      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-27T19:20:04Z",
      "note": "Reviewed all four publicly identified attack receipts and senders, the current exploit trace, verified MinterProxyV2 source, deployment and code history, exact victim transfers, the commit-pinned reproduction, and historical price evidence. The first three transactions belong to attacker 0x6eec0f4c017afe3dfadf32b51339c37e9fd59dfb and helper 0x791c6542bc52efe4f20df0ee672b88579ae3fd9a; this record is the independent later campaign by 0xacdbe7b770a14ca3bc34865ac3986c0ce771fd68 and helper 0x52b19de39476823d33ab4b1edbec91e29dadba38. The 373-frame trace calls MinterProxyV2.swap() 29 times. Each call uses the attacker helper as the fake token to satisfy input and output checks, then has MinterProxyV2 call transferFrom on a victim token. The target is direct, not a proxy: its 16,759-byte runtime hashes to 0xecf05feba4556785408c6165fe0f1cbb81c7e4b3286832110b75ee69ce9ad175 at deployment block 37761305 and pre-exploit block 37881403, has zero EIP-1967 implementation and beacon slots, contains no SELFDESTRUCT or DELEGATECALL, and makes no target-originated DELEGATECALL in the exploit trace. Code age is 361,079 seconds. The receipt records 29 exact victim-to-attacker asset transfers; contemporaneous pre-exploit quotes value them at $133,020.54221111373."
    },
